t_candidate_committed_past_checkpoint`, and the repair is `git reset --soft <checkpoint_oid>` before completing again.\n\n## Change Request Under Review\n\n- Change Request: `CR-TASK-260830-2atgj4-2` revision `2` (state `ready`)\n- Element: `TASK-260830-2atgj4`, integration scope: `STORY-260830-1oqfec`\n- Branch: `task-board/story/STORY-260830-1oqfec`\n- Base OID: `e4e3e8834675cf3814effd3b2673b4931dfbf311`\n- Candidate tree OID: `92d7da93a719d80810895e2ce5cfaf1c23ce68c7`\n- Repository delta: `present`\n- Patch resource: `TASK-260830-2atgj4_change-request_rev2.patch` (sha256 `3e29cfe232c8f258f332eae4b00c2738309e4fb78b9a4026e2de7a03e066a138`)\n\n```bash\ngit -C . diff e4e3e8834675cf3814effd3b2673b4931dfbf311 92d7da93a719d80810895e2ce5cfaf1c23ce68c7          # the exact reviewable delta\ngit -C . diff --stat e4e3e8834675cf3814effd3b2673b4931dfbf311 92d7da93a719d80810895e2ce5cfaf1c23ce68c7   # its shape\n```\n\nChanged paths (37):\n\n- `LOGBOOK.md`\n- `README.md`\n- `internal/fencing/TRACEABILITY.md`\n- `internal/fencing/census_test.go`\n- `internal/fencing/codes_test.go`\n- `internal/fencing/doc.go`\n- `internal/fencing/fixtures_test.go`\n- `internal/fencing/gate.go`\n- `internal/fencing/gate_test.go`\n- `internal/fencing/ownership_properties_test.go`\n- `internal/fencing/scenarios_test.go`\n- `internal/fencing/terminate.go`\n- `internal/fencing/terminate_test.go`\n- `internal/fencing/testdata/forge/forge.go`\n- `internal/fencing/testdata/mutate.py`\n- `internal/fencing/testdata/use/use.go`\n- `internal/fencing/token.go`\n- `internal/fencing/token_test.go`\n- `internal/sessquery/lease_store_adopt_test.go`\n- `internal/sessrepo/TRACEABILITY.md`\n- `internal/sessrepo/census_test.go`\n- `internal/sessrepo/doc.go`\n- `internal/sessrepo/lease.go`\n- `internal/sessrepo/lease_crash_test.go`\n- `internal/sessrepo/lease_properties_test.go`\n- `internal/sessrepo/lease_store.go`\n- `internal/sessrepo/lease_store_test.go`\n- `internal/sessrepo/sessrepo.go`\n- `internal/sessrepo/testdata/mutate.py`\n- `internal/sessstate/census_state_test.go`\n- `internal/sessstate/ownership_properties_test.go`\n- `internal/sessstate/sessstate.go`\n- `internal/sessstate/testdata/mutate_properties.py`\n- `internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck/main_test.go`\n- `internal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json`\n- `internal/traceability/traceability.go`\n- `internal/traceability/traceability_test.go`\n\n### Recording the verdict\n\nAcceptance is a named mutation, not a status change:\n\n```bash\ntask-board m 'accept_cr(TASK-260830-2atgj4, revision=2, evidence=TASK-260830-2atgj4_review-verdict-rev2.md)'\n```\n\n`accept_cr` writes `accepted` and `integrating` atomically: the Change Request becomes `accepted`, this run is stamped as the reviewer, and TASK-260830-2atgj4 routes the element to `integrating` — accepted but not landed, and never `done`. The accepted revision is bound to its producer role and archetype (`developer`/`implementer`), and only a new tracked run with that exact producer role and archetype may checkpoint or integrate it. The orchestrator routes that run; it does not close the leaf, and no orchestrator run may execute the integration itself. `done` is produced only by the integration transaction, never by you and never by an acknowledgement. Never supply `commit_ack` yourself.\n\nChanges requested and Stop-The-Line are unchanged: route to `to-dev`/`analysis` or evidence-backed `blocked`. Leaving the element in `reviewing` is still not a verdict and still gets this run cancelled and respawned.\n"}}
