ale and same-epoch loser preservation — a losing lease (lower epoch, or same epoch losing the tuple order) is never dropped, rewritten or promoted; its history remains visible as divergent/conflict evidence after any sequence of unions, force takeovers and reconnects, (3) clock non-authority — created_at and any wall-clock member never influence the winner, the fencing decision or the parked/refused outcome (shift every timestamp arbitrarily, including backwards and equal, and assert identical verdicts), (4) zero duplicate authorized owners — after any admissible sequence, at most one lease is authoritative per logical session and per epoch, and the fencing gates admit exactly that one; two hosts or two processes can never both pass an activation-class gate for the same session. Use Go's testing/quick or rapid-style generators you write yourself (no new module dependency unless the go-testing-tools skill lists one; then justify) over a closed small alphabet (epochs 1..4, holders a/b/c, lease ids x/y/z, hosts h1/h2, event kinds the landed shapes admit) with exhaustive enumeration where the space is small (state it) and bounded random exploration with a fixed seed and a recorded iteration count otherwise; every property must be falsified by at least one narrowing mutant of the production reducer (winner tie-break inverted; loser dropped from the union; created_at consulted; a second authoritative owner admitted at the same epoch) executed by a shipped harness with per-plant raw logs, subprocess exits and an applied harmless SURVIVED control — a property that no plant can falsify is not evidence. Also add the P3 vector from the 3g12yp verdict (TestAuthorizeRefusesMalformedPresented: {session A, epoch 0, valid third lease} expecting invalid_arguments) and reword the stale section:17.2 gap prose to its narrower reader-enum meaning if the registry is touched. No product behavior change is expected; if a property exposes a defect, fix it minimally with a RED-first regression and say so. This is the FINAL leaf (story_final CR): carry the Story-close items — traceability registry acceptance cases for the four properties bound to the real reducers with honest coverage text, reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256 re-pinned; README sections for internal/fencing (if missing) and the property suite with test commands and no capability claim; LOGBOOK entry. Managed Story worktree contract: .temp/STORY-260830-1oqfec/worktree on branch task-board/story/STORY-260830-1oqfec whose tip is the 3g12yp checkpoint; leave the candidate UNCOMMITTED, never commit on the Story branch, never edit .task-board directly, never self-accept; if origin/main moves before your handoff (it will: a release-agnostic validation command is landing on trunk), run task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260830-2atgj4 and restore any trunk-changed path the refresh left stale with a single-path git checkout HEAD -- <path> (task-board.config.json in particular must equal HEAD); before handoff verify git status shows only candidate paths (no __pycache__, no .pyc). Evidence contract as in the repository DoD; conformance matrix mapping each invariant and clause to a property, its generator domain, its falsifying mutant and the observed exits. Read the Curator-managed go-testing-tools skill first; all CI local; run the full configured validation suite once before the handoff; hand off no later than 3 hours in. Attach TASK-260830-2atgj4_results.md, TASK-260830-2atgj4_conformance-matrix.md and TASK-260830-2atgj4_producer-evidence.tar.gz (a real gzip archive), keep the checklist current, then task-board handoff TASK-260830-2atgj4 --role developer and exit promptly. Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board. Model: muse-spark max. The independent reviewer will be muse-spark xhigh while codex is out of quota.","final_result":true}}}
