{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c601","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae9c-cde9-7503-b771-d867bf2eff64"},"sequence":347,"recorded_at":1780531400000689,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"c50b0c1e-3e8f-47ac-b724-ccf66299a997","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"c50b0c1e-3e8f-47ac-b724-ccf66299a997","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"c50b0c1e-3e8f-47ac-b724-ccf66299a997"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ae9d-8cc1-73b1-8d72-6b25b76430b7"},"task_id":"01a0ae9d-8cc1-73b1-8d72-6b25b76430b7","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ae9d-8cc1-73b1-8d72-6b25b76430b7","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260830-2atgj4/TASK-260830-2atgj4_results.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-2atgj4 results: property-test the ownership reducer (final leaf)\n2|\n3|Role: developer. Worktree: `.temp/STORY-260830-1oqfec/worktree` on\n4|`task-board/story/STORY-260830-1oqfec`, candidate left UNCOMMITTED\n5|for the handoff snapshot. Status at handoff: ready for review.\n6|\n7|## Outcome\n8|\n9|The four story-pinned ownership invariants hold as 11 executable\n10|property tests over the landed production reducers\n11|(`sessstate.Reduce`/`Compare`, `sessrepo.WinningLease`/`ListLeases`,\n12|`fencing.Authorize*`), with hand-written closed-alphabet generators\n13|(no new module dependency), exhaustive enumeration where the space is\n14|small, and bounded seeded-random exploration otherwise. The\n15|union-order property exposed one genuine defect on the landed\n16|reducer and fixed it minimally with a RED-first regression (below).\n17|The falsification battery kills 8 narrowing plants through the named\n18|properties with an applied harmless SURVIVED control. Story-close\n19|items are carried: three traceability acceptance cases bound to the\n20|real reducers with honest coverage text and a re-pinned registry\n21|digest, the section:17.2 gap reword, the 3g12yp P3 vector, README and\n22|LOGBOOK updates, and the full configured validation suite green.\n23|\n24|## AC coverage: 18 of 18 rows driven, 0 stated bounds on behavior\n25|\n26|Every row is driven through the production entry point by a named\n27|committed test. Crash/idempotency: the changed derivation\n28|(`resolveWinner`) is pure with no durable mutation, so no new crash\n29|window exists; the landed lease crash/idempotency tests remain green\n30|(batch A). No unsupported capability is advertised (claims gate\n31|green; README adds no `ax`, `doctor`, or runtime claim).\n32|\n33|| # | AC row | Production call site | Named test(s) |\n34|| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n35|| 1 | Union permutations project byte-identically | `sessstate.Reduce` | `TestOwnershipUnionOrderIndependent`, `TestOwnershipUnionOrderRegression` |\n36|| 2 | Successive-union partitions project byte-identically | `sessstate.Reduce` | `TestOwnershipUnionPartitionStable` |\n37|| 3 | Stale (lower-epoch) loser never dropped/rewritten/promoted | `sessstate.Reduce`; `sessrepo.GetLease`, `ListLeases` | `TestOwnershipLoserHistoryPreserved`, `TestOwnershipStoreLoserBytesPreserved` |\n38|| 4 | Same-epoch loser never dropped/rewritten/promoted, tie named | `sessstate.Reduce` | `TestOwnershipLoserHistoryPreserved` |\n39|| 5 | Winner is the greatest tuple; `Compare` is the total order | `sessstate.Compare` | `TestOwnershipWinnerIsTupleMaximum` |\n40|| 6 | `created_at` never influences store authority or fencing verdicts | `sessrepo.CreateLease`, `CompareAndSwapLease`, `WinningLease`, `VerifyFencingToken` | `TestOwnershipStoreClockNonAuthority` |\n41|| 7 | Absolute wall-clock position never influences gate verdicts | `fencing.Authorize*` (all five entries) | `TestOwnershipGateClockNonAuthority` |\n42|| 8 | At most one authoritative lease per session and epoch | `sessrepo.WinningLease`, `ListLeases`, `CompareAndSwapLease`, `GetLease` | `TestOwnershipStoreSingleAuthorityPerEpoch` |\n43|| 9 | Gates admit exactly the winner; pairwise exclusion | `fencing.Authorize*` (all five entries) | `TestOwnershipGateSingleAuthorizedOwner` |\n44|| 10 | Two handles/processes share one head; lagging CAS refuses stale | `sessrepo.CompareAndSwapLease`, `WinningLease` | `TestOwnershipStoreTwoHandlesOneHead` |\n45|| 11 | Exact contract fixtures pass | All entries above | Full suite green (batches A/B/C, 27 packages) |\n46|| 12 | Negative/refusal cases pass | All gates above | Full suite green; landed negatives untouched and green |\n47|| 13 | Crash/idempotency evidence where durable state mutates | (no new durable mutation) | Landed `TestCrashBeforeLeaseWriteIsSafeRetry`, `TestCrashAfterLeaseCommitCountsAsCommitted`, idempotent-retry tests green |\n48|| 14 | No unsupported capability advertised | README scan posture | `TestRealREADMECarriesNoPositiveClaim` et al. green |\n49|| 15 | P3 vector: epoch-zero third lease refuses `invalid_arguments` | `fencing.Authorize*` (all five entries) | `TestAuthorizeRefusesMalformedPresented/epoch_zero_other_lease` |\n50|| 16 | section:17.2 gap reworded to the narrower reader-enum meaning | `internal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json` | `go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck` exit 0 |\n51|| 17 | Traceability cases bound with honest coverage, digest re-pinned | Registry + `reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256` | `TestVerifyRepositoryAcceptsExactOwnership` (113 cases), tracecheck pins |\n52|| 18 | Every property falsified by a narrowing mutant with controls | `internal/sessstate/testdata/mutate_properties.py` | 8 KILLED by named properties; harmless SURVIVED; harness exit 0 |\n53|\n54|## Defect found by the property (RED-first)\n55|\n56|`resolveWinner` reported each losing union lease against the transient\n57|arrival-order winner: with union `{R@1, A@1}` on an empty chain, one\n58|arrival order records R's loss and the other drops it entirely, and\n59|multi-entry unions name different losers-to targets per order. The\n60|winner was always right; the divergent-history evidence was not a\n61|function of the multiset. Fix (`internal/sessstate/sessstate.go`\n62|only): select the greatest tuple in a first pass, then report every\n63|entry below it in ascending tuple order naming the final winner, with\n64|the off-chain flag recomputed from the final winner (proven\n65|equivalent to the tracked flag in all cases). RED: 4 of 5 property\n66|tests fail on the landed code (`red-ownership-properties.log`).\n67|GREEN: 5 of 5 pass after the fix (`green-ownership-properties.log`).\n68|All landed union assertions were order-free, so the only collateral\n69|was the refusal-census line pins (sessstate.go:924/927 to :929/:932).\n70|\n71|## Files changed (candidate, uncommitted)\n72|\n73|- `internal/sessstate/sessstate.go`: two-pass `resolveWinner` (the fix).\n74|- `internal/sessstate/ownership_properties_test.go` (new): P1/P2\n75|  properties (5 tests).\n76|- `internal/sessrepo/lease_properties_test.go` (new): P3/P4 store\n77|  properties (4 tests).\n78|- `internal/fencing/ownership_properties_test.go` (new): P3/P4 gate\n79|  properties (2 tests).\n80|- `internal/fencing/gate_test.go`: P3 vector\n81|  `epoch_zero_other_lease`.\n82|- `internal/sessstate/testdata/mutate_properties.py` (new): the\n83|  falsification battery.\n84|- `internal/sessstate/census_state_test.go`: census line re-pin.\n85|- `internal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json`,\n86|  `internal/traceability/traceability.go` (digest re-pin),\n87|  `internal/traceability/traceability_test.go` (113),\n88|  `internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck/main_test.go` (113 x2):\n89|  registry story-close.\n90|- `README.md`: property-suite section, harness table row, 113 figure.\n91|- `LOGBOOK.md`: task entry.\n92|\n93|## Validation (all local, real exits, this tree)\n94|\n95|- `go vet ./...`: exit 0. `GOOS=windows go vet ./...`: exit 0.\n96|  `gofmt -l internal`: empty. `go build ./...`: exit 0.\n97|  `GOOS=windows go build ./...`: exit 0.\n98|- `go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck`: exit 0\n99|  (`acceptance_cases=113`, `clauses_discharged=28/485`).\n100|- Catalog directive pinned (1 exact `//go:generate`) +\n101|  `go generate ./internal/catalog` + clean diff: exit 0.\n102|- cigate contract gates (6 tests) and claim gates (6 tests): all PASS.\n103|- Test batches A (sessstate/sessrepo/fencing/sessquery), B (12 pkgs),\n104|  C (11 pkgs): 27/27 `ok`, 0 FAIL.\n105|- Race batches (same splits): 27/27 `ok`, no `DATA RACE`.\n106|- Coverage batches: every package reports a number; sessstate 92.4%,\n107|  sessrepo 86.6%, fencing 97.5% (reported, no floor).\n108|- Fixture matrix: secprim 51 PASS, secconftest 59 PASS, skips loud.\n109|- Fuzz smoke: 13/13 derived targets print `fuzz: elapsed`.\n110|- Mutant battery: 8 KILLED by named properties, harmless SURVIVED,\n111|  harness exit 0.\n112|- `git status` at handoff: only the 13 candidate paths above (plus\n113|  ignored `.temp/` evidence); no `__pycache__`, no `.pyc`.\n114|\n115|## Trunk drift (refresh-candidate outcome)\n116|\n117|`origin/main` moved during the run from `62d4463` to `e4e3e88`\n118|(STORY-260917-158jyi: release-agnostic cataloggen `-adopted` check,\n119|plus its board-state record). `task-board worktree refresh-candidate\n120|TASK-260830-2atgj4` replays the story checkpoints in isolation and\n121|stops at a mechanical LOGBOOK append-append conflict at the 2f5393\n122|replay (trunk's 3lt2xv entry vs the 2f5393 entry, both under\n123|`## 2026-09-17`); trunk's entry is newer (11:05 vs 09:17 UTC+4), so\n124|the correct resolution keeps trunk's entry on top. The\n125|`--replay-resolutions` file schema is not documented on any surface\n126|available here: `path`/`sha256(base64 content)` parse, but every\n127|checkpoint-binding field name tried is refused as unknown while the\n128|binding itself is required (`replay resolution checkpoint is outside\n129|the original sequence`). The candidate worktree is verified intact\n130|(HEAD `1b8e75a`, all 13 candidate paths, `task-board.config.json`\n131|unmodified and equal to HEAD). Integration is the orchestrator's\n132|step; notes for it: (a) trunk touches none of my Go paths (only\n133|`internal/catalog*`, board files, README catalog rows, one LOGBOOK\n134|entry); (b) the only same-file adjacencies are LOGBOOK top (keep all four\n135|entries, newest-first by wall time: this 2atgj4 entry, trunk 3lt2xv\n136|11:05, 3g12yp 11:01, 2f5393 09:17, all UTC+4 2026-09-17) and the\n137|README tools table (trunk rewrote the Go-toolchain\n138|row's cataloggen command; I add a new row after the fencing row —\n139|keep both); (c) my evidence quotes the `-adopted`-neutral commands\n140|only (`go generate`, tracecheck), never command 21's explicit form.\n141|\n142|## Evidence attached\n143|\n144|- `TASK-260830-2atgj4_results.md` (this file)\n145|- `TASK-260830-2atgj4_conformance-matrix.md`\n146|- `TASK-260830-2atgj4_producer-evidence.tar.gz` (real gzip: RED/GREEN\n147|  logs, affected-package logs, validation batch logs, coverage logs,\n148|  mutants/ raw logs + mutants.json)","final_result":true}}}
