{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c653","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae9c-cde9-7503-b771-d867bf2eff64"},"sequence":388,"recorded_at":1780531400000771,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"c50b0c1e-3e8f-47ac-b724-ccf66299a997","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"c50b0c1e-3e8f-47ac-b724-ccf66299a997","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"c50b0c1e-3e8f-47ac-b724-ccf66299a997"},"call_id":"call_01a0ae9d930f74fbaf06b7e060865872","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260830-2f5393/TASK-260830-2f5393_review-verdict-rev1.md`.\n1|# Review verdict — TASK-260830-2f5393 rev1 (implement lease record validation and CAS)\n2|\n3|## Verdict: ACCEPT revision 1\n4|\n5|Change Request `CR-TASK-260830-2f5393-1` revision 1 is accepted for\n6|integration. One P2 finding (stale ownership-registry gap row, §6 below)\n7|is recorded with an explicit story-level requirement; it does not\n8|invalidate this leaf. No P1 deviation was found. The candidate was never\n9|mutated: every probe ran in isolated copies under `/tmp/review-2f5393/`\n10|or as read-only `go test`/`go vet` on the live tree. No commit,\n11|checkpoint, or branch operation was performed.\n12|\n13|- Candidate source integrity: `sha256 internal/sessrepo/lease_store.go =\n14|  bdb89cb607268d1d06ac2eb235f4e1a22017d3da61899203be26d15153cac6c8`\n15|  (equals the battery-time digest), `testdata/mutate.py =\n16|  a9d795ce50ae4d17c746a9c66bc9256a37902b82f0a76d78a3e8d2ee07290e5c`.\n17|- AC coverage: **8 of 8 AC rows driven** through the named production\n18|  entries (`Repository.CreateLease`, `Repository.CompareAndSwapLease`,\n19|  `Repository.VerifyFencingToken`, `CheckFencingExpiry`,\n20|  `Repository.WinningLease`/`ListLeases`/`GetLease`, `AttestLeaseRecord`);\n21|  public-CLI coverage 0 of 8 by stated bound (no `ax` command exists).\n22|\n23|## 1. Spec fidelity\n24|\n25|- Pinned text (§5.3): \"There is no time-expiring ownership lease in\n26|  v0.5.0. Liveness is not authority.\" `lease_expired` occurs **0 times**\n27|  in `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`, and the §15.3 taxonomy names\n28|  `lease_conflict` (exit 10) but no expired-lease class. The\n29|  grant-expiry-only design (`fencing_grant_expired`, lease never\n30|  retires) is faithful; `TestLeaseNeverExpiresWithAge` pins it. A new\n31|  operational code is permitted (\"New error codes MAY be added in a\n32|  compatible minor contract version\"). Not a deviation.\n33|- Task scope cites v0.5.0 numbering; the retained v0.6.0 headings (§2.2,\n34|  §5.3, §13.6–13.10) exist verbatim in the pinned document. The only\n35|  numbering difference observed is the retained sentence above, which\n36|  still says \"v0.5.0\" inside the v0.6.0 text.\n37|- `internal/sessquery/lease.go` sha256 is identical trunk-vs-candidate\n38|  (`3ce19568…ec2f`); `winningLeaseFor` is byte-unchanged. The adoption\n39|  test (`TestLeaseStoreRecordsAdmitWithoutBehavioralChange`) proves\n40|  store-minted records admit there with equal digest/epoch/lease/holder.\n41|- `CompareLeaseTuple` restates `sessstate.Compare` line-for-line for the\n42|  comparison logic. The agreement corpus is **6 example pairs, not an\n43|  exhaustive alphabet** (`lease_store_adopt_test.go:66-73`). Planting a\n44|  reversed tie-break on the sessrepo side goes RED\n45|  (`attacks/A4-compare-divergence.log`, exit 1).\n46|\n47|## 2. CAS, epochs, holder, fencing (10/10 reviewer probes green)\n48|\n49|Probes in `probes/reviewer_probe_test.go`, log\n50|`probes/reviewer-probes.log` (exit 0). Findings:\n51|\n52|- No API accepts an epoch: succession always derives `head.Epoch+1`\n53|  (never skips, never decreases); three successions pin epochs 2–4 with\n54|  a linked predecessor chain. A second epoch-1 create refuses\n55|  `lease_exists` (`TestReviewerSecondCreateAtSameEpochRefuses`).\n56|- Sequential race on one basis: first CAS wins; the loser's differing\n57|  bytes refuse **`stale_lease_epoch`**, not `lease_conflict`\n58|  (`TestReviewerSequentialRaceOnSameBasis`). Correction to the review\n59|  brief: `lease_conflict` is returned only for expectations naming\n60|  nothing known (malformed/empty/foreign); a superseded-but-known basis\n61|  with differing bytes is stale. The behavior is spec-consistent\n62|  (loser does not win) and covered by narrowing mutant N-cas-stale.\n63|- Byte-identical replay of a committed CAS returns the same reference\n64|  with the blob directory byte-identical (name+size map unchanged).\n65|- Replay of an old successor after the head advanced further still\n66|  answers the persisted successor (re-mint against the pre-commit basis\n67|  hits); it does not refuse (`TestReviewerReplayAfterHeadAdvanced`).\n68|  Correction to the review brief's \"(refused)\": replay-after-advance is\n69|  a safe answer, refusal applies only to differing bytes (stale).\n70|- Holder is host-UUIDv7 only: same-host re-presentation verifies; the\n71|  stored record carries no `pid`/`process_id`/`start_time`/`boot_id`/\n72|  `holder_token` field. Same host + different process verifies (no\n73|  process binding exists to reject it); there is no pid/start/boot\n74|  material to survive a restart — holder identity is the host UUID\n75|  alone, per §2.2 inv 4–5.\n76|- Older-epoch token after a newer lease → `stale_lease_epoch`.\n77|  Same-epoch tampered lease ID with valid v4 grammar → `lease_conflict`;\n78|  tampered version nibble (v5) → `invalid lease record`.\n79|- `R-cas-epoch-skip` (head+1 → head+2) KILLED twice by the successor\n80|  and monotonicity suites.\n81|\n82|## 3. Durability\n83|\n84|- Split brain probed by unioning two partitioned epoch-2 blobs:\n85|  `ListLeases` holds 3 blobs (1, 2, 2′), `WinningLease` elects the\n86|  bytewise-greater lease ID deterministically, the loser is preserved\n87|  and its token no longer verifies\n88|  (`TestReviewerSplitBrainUnionElectsGreaterLease`).\n89|- Staged-but-unrenamed temp is ignored by load; an `AfterLeaseStage`\n90|  fault leaves no final and the retry lands the exact epoch. A tampered\n91|  final blob refuses `chain_corrupt` through both `ListLeases` and\n92|  `GetLease` funnels.\n93|- Injector crash suites plus real-SIGKILL rename-seam drills\n94|  (create + cas) rerun **twice**, exit 0 both runs\n95|  (`probes/crash-rerun-1.log`, `crash-rerun-2.log`).\n96|\n97|## 4. Refusal census (26 sites, 7 new sentinels)\n98|\n99|`grep -c \"refuse(Err\" lease_store.go` = 26, matching the 26 narrowing\n100|plants (23 new-sentinel sites + 3 `ErrChainCorrupt` funnel sites).\n101|Census markers: 7 new boundary markers; equality ledger: 3 rows.\n102|Attacks, each exit 1 with logs in `attacks/`:\n103|\n104|- A1 (remove `\").VerifyFencingToken\"` marker): RED — 7 sites reported\n105|  \"never reached beneath a production boundary entry\".\n106|- A2 (swap conditions of two adjacent same-class grammar arms,\n107|  v4↔v7): RED — `TestCreateLeasePersistsEpochOneCreate` fails.\n108|- A3 (one refuse call stretched across two lines): RED — the\n109|  line-anchored equality ledger mismatches (`lease_store.go:650` →\n110|  `:651`); the refusal-derivation gate additionally requires\n111|  single-line calls.\n112|\n113|## 5. Mutation\n114|\n115|- Producer battery rerun in an isolated copy on the exact final source:\n116|  exit 0 — **27/27 applied plants KILLED** (26 narrowing + 1\n117|  token-preserving `T-create-time-pad`); harmless control SURVIVED;\n118|  NOT_APPLIED and COMPILE_OR_HARNESS_FAILURE classified separately\n119|  (`verify/producer-battery-rerun-mutants.json` + `verify/per-plant/`\n120|  raw logs).\n121|- Reviewer-owned mutants on producer-unmutated arms, each KILLED twice\n122|  (`own-mutants/per-plant/`, runner `own-mutants/reviewer_mutate.py`):\n123|  R-expiry-boundary (`>` → `>=`, boundary grant must stay current),\n124|  R-cas-epoch-skip (head+1 → head+2), R-fence-lease-directional (tie\n125|  break admits only lesser IDs; the greater-ID loser then verifies),\n126|  R-fence-holder-prefix (holder weakened to 8-char prefix); applied\n127|  harmless comment control SURVIVED twice; control-after full package\n128|  green. Honest note: a first prefix variant for the lease tie-break\n129|  SURVIVED because the suite's winner/loser IDs share no 8-char prefix\n130|  (too narrow to admit — not counted); the directional replacement\n131|  above is the accepted evidence.\n132|- Fail-closed mint confirmed from `N-create-token.log`: the admitted\n133|  `not-a-uuid` token dies in mint with a plain operational error\n134|  (\"identify lease record: invalid canonical object identity…\"),\n135|  changing the refusal class — mint failures are operational errors,\n136|  never refusals.\n137|\n138|## 6. Bounds, docs, registry\n139|\n140|- Provhost 5-site attestation bound holds: `go test\n141|  ./internal/provhost` green (includes\n142|  `TestNoProductionPathAttestsProviderIdentityBinding`); lease_store.go\n143|  contains no direct `VerifyObjectIdentity` call (one comment mention).\n144|- Added docs (`README.md`, `doc.go`, `LOGBOOK.md`, `TRACEABILITY.md`)\n145|  claim the §5.3 lifecycle as implemented while\n146|  `internal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json` section:5.3 still\n147|  carries the gap \"lease acquisition, renewal, expiry and fencing are\n148|  not implemented\". **P2** per the review brief. Requirement: a later\n149|  leaf of STORY-260830-1oqfec must update the section:5.3 binding and\n150|  re-pin `reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256` before story_final\n151|  (precedent: Stories 3drr2m, 3jqsx1, 3m2mw8, 2jylym). No CLI, doctor,\n152|  or capability claim exists in the candidate (added text explicitly\n153|  disclaims all three).\n154|\n155|## 7. Hygiene and suites\n156|\n157|- Changed paths are exactly the 12 candidate paths (6 modified + 6 new:\n158|  `lease_store.go`, `lease_store_test.go`, `lease_crash_test.go`,\n159|  `TRACEABILITY.md`, `lease_store_adopt_test.go`, `testdata/mutate.py`);\n160|  no `__pycache__`/`.pyc`, no `task-board.config.json`, no stray\n161|  plants; work left UNCOMMITTED.\n162|- `go vet ./...` exit 0; `gofmt` clean; `tracecheck` exit 0\n163|  (contracts=63 sections=36 cases=101 fixtures=32);\n164|  `cataloggen -check` exit 0.\n165|- Suites rerun by the reviewer, exit 0: `go test ./internal/sessrepo\n166|  ./internal/provhost -count=1`; `sessquery -run Lease`;\n167|  `sessrepo -race`; `provhost -race`. Full `-count=1` runs of\n168|  sessrepo/sessquery/sessstate/provhost observed exit 0 (background\n169|  run; logs not retained). Full `-race` over all 26 packages and the\n170|  fuzz/cross-compile matrix accepted from the attached producer\n171|  evidence (`full-race.log` in\n172|  `TASK-260830-2f5393_producer-evidence.tar.gz`).","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c655","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae9c-cde9-7503-b771-d867bf2eff64"},"sequence":389,"recorded_at":1780531400000773,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"c50b0c1e-3e8f-47ac-b724-ccf66299a997","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"c50b0c1e-3e8f-47ac-b724-ccf66299a997","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"c50b0c1e-3e8f-47ac-b724-ccf66299a997"},"call_id":"call_01a0ae9d942374d88d916a4ef032d182","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260830-3g12yp/TASK-260830-3g12yp_review-verdict-rev1.md`.\n1|# Review verdict — TASK-260830-3g12yp rev1: implement provider and pane fencing gates\n2|\n3|Verdict: **ACCEPT** (revision 1). Route: `accept_cr(TASK-260830-3g12yp, revision=1,\n4|evidence=TASK-260830-3g12yp_review-verdict-rev1.md)`.\n5|\n6|Reviewer ran headless in the managed Story worktree at base `0ebb7fa` with the\n7|candidate applied uncommitted. All probes were isolated immutable copies; the\n8|live worktree, index, branch, and HEAD were never mutated. Scratch harnesses\n9|live outside the repo under `/tmp/rev-3g12yp/`; per-plant raw logs and\n10|subprocess exits are in the attached\n11|`TASK-260830-3g12yp_review-evidence-rev1.tar.gz`.\n12|\n13|## 1. Spec fidelity — confirmed\n14|\n15|Pinned authority `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`, quoted independently:\n16|\n17|- 2.2#1–#4 (lines 408–413): exactly one winning lease; replica MUST NOT\n18|  launch/resume/accept input; every owner event carries winning epoch+lease;\n19|  peers reject lower/losing events into a divergent branch. Gated by\n20|  `Authorize*` (`internal/fencing/gate.go`) plus the predecessor's\n21|  `AppendEvent`/projector preservation, driven by\n22|  `TestAuthorizeAdmitsWinnerExactEpochAllOperations`,\n23|  `TestAuthorizeParksAndRefusesRemote`,\n24|  `TestOldOwnerReconnectRejectedAfterForceTakeover`.\n25|- 5.3 tuple rule (lines 1954–1968): greatest `(epoch, lease_id)`, bytewise\n26|  UUID order; revalidation before input/turn/checkpoint/push/resume\n27|  (line 1970). Exact-equality enforcement in `Authorize` lines 356–375;\n28|  expiry reused from `sessrepo.CheckFencingExpiry`, never restated.\n29|- Section 4 wrapper rule (lines 1366–1372, 1418+): compare local fencing\n30|  token before launch; park when remote/ambiguous/unverified; terminate only\n31|  for explicit force recovery after preserving diagnostics.\n32|  `AuthorizeRestore`/`AuthorizeActivation` park; `AuthorizeTerminateStale`\n33|  (`internal/fencing/terminate.go`) authorizes only fenced targets under\n34|  force+diagnostics and refuses the live owner.\n35|- 7.5 `LeaseToken` (line 2952): `{session_id, lease_epoch, lease_id}` minted\n36|  only from a passed gate (`mintLeaseToken`, sole `&leaseSealToken{}` site in\n37|  `token.go`), bound to quiesce/capture/materialize via `Bind`.\n38|- Park vocabulary (line 1799): `remote_owner|stale_owner|restore_policy|\n39|  failed_handoff` + winning lease ID — exact `ParkReason` constants and\n40|  `ParkDetails` extraction.\n41|- Section 15.2 exits (lines ~14849/15.2 table): 10 =\n42|  `not_owner,stale_owner,lease_conflict`; 2 = `invalid_arguments`; 3 =\n43|  `local_precondition_failed`. The producer's 10/10/10/2/3 claim reproduced:\n44|  `TestGateRefusalsUseRegisteredCodes` green in my run, and every park\n45|  unwraps to its registered cause (`TestParkDecisionCarriesSection15Cause`).\n46|  `ErrParked` is a decision marker, never a new class: `park()` always wraps\n47|  a registered cause. No new class minted anywhere (only the six sentinels).\n48|\n49|## 2. Refusal census — 28 of 28 arms driven through production entries\n50|\n51|`Authorize` core, 18 arms, each reached through all five entries by a named\n52|test: unknown operation, presented session/epoch/lease grammar (3),\n53|foreign session, absent winner, winner grammar, unverified, ambiguous,\n54|failed handoff, missing grant, missing clock, expired grant, unusable policy,\n55|remote direction, lower epoch, ahead epoch, lease mismatch.\n56|`AuthorizeTerminateStale`, 8 arms with 8 named tests (malformed target,\n57|garbage winner, no winner, no force, no diagnostics, foreign session,\n58|live owner at epochs 1 and 2, fenced-target authorization).\n59|`LeaseToken.Bind`, 2 arms (forged/zero seal, unknown operation).\n60|Ratio: **28 of 28 refusal/park arms driven; 18 of 18 AC rows driven, 0 of 18\n61|as a public CLI by stated ownership bound** (no `ax` session command exists;\n62|takeover/fork/stop/resume are modeled callers).\n63|\n64|Taxonomy attacks (isolated copies, raw logs attached):\n65|\n66|- Swap: exchanged the adjacent Ambiguous/HandoffFailed conditions. KILLED by\n67|  the existing suites on both sides\n68|  (`TestAuthorizeParksAndRefusesAmbiguous/activation/verified`,\n69|  `TestAuthorizeParksAndRefusesFailedHandoff/activation/verified`, …).\n70|  My both-flags probe passes on the clean tree, pinning precedence\n71|  (ambiguity first) — log `own/A-swapped-*.log`.\n72|- Swallow (one-token class change, stale→conflict on lower epoch): KILLED by\n73|  `TestAuthorizeRefusesLowerEpoch` — log `own/B.log`.\n74|- Delete park branch (remote launch park→hard refusal): KILLED by\n75|  `TestAuthorizeParksAndRefusesRemote` — log `own/C.log`.\n76|\n77|## 3. Behavioral probes — admitted/refused/parked with exact class\n78|\n79|Own-plant matrix through the production entries (isolated copies):\n80|\n81|- Lower epoch by one and by many: `stale_owner` (non-launch) / park\n82|  `stale_owner` (launch) — existing vectors plus precedence probe.\n83|- Same-epoch loser, lease sorting before and after the winner\n84|  (`fenceLeaseC`, `fenceLeaseC2`): `lease_conflict` / park `stale_owner`.\n85|- Foreign session with winner's epoch (prefix-sharing B, fully foreign C):\n86|  `lease_conflict` on all entries.\n87|- Expired grant at boundary second: boundary-fresh (exactly interval) mints;\n88|  +1s refuses `lease_conflict`; zero policy refuses `invalid_arguments`.\n89|- Absent lease with verified/unverified sync: park `restore_policy` (empty\n90|  winner) on launch, `lease_conflict` elsewhere; `Observe` reports absence\n91|  as data, unknown session propagates `ErrUnknownSession`.\n92|- Ambiguous, remote (prefix-sharing and fully remote holders), unverified:\n93|  park with exact reason + `not_owner`/`lease_conflict` cause, or hard\n94|  refusal off-launch.\n95|- Old-owner reconnect after force takeover: old token refuses `stale_owner`\n96|  (input/mutation/checkpoint), parks `remote_owner` on the old wrapper;\n97|  losing events preserved without application; union reports\n98|  losing-branch-preserved with authoritative state standing.\n99|- Concurrent force takeovers: bytewise-greater lease wins in either union\n100|  order; loser stops accepting input with `lease_conflict`.\n101|- Minted token replayed across operations: stable triple on\n102|  quiesce/capture/materialize from every entry; unknown operation\n103|  (`bogus,resume,stop`) refuses `invalid_arguments`.\n104|- Token bound for epoch N after CAS to N+1: old token stale/remote-refused,\n105|  rival token authorizes (`TestAuthorizeEndToEndOverRepository`).\n106|\n107|## 4. Forgery bound — confirmed, plus one extra census-scope probe\n108|\n109|- `go build ./internal/fencing/testdata/use` exits 0; `go build\n110|  ./internal/fencing/testdata/forge` fails with\n111|  `cannot refer to unexported field seal` (rerun by reviewer).\n112|- `TestLeaseTokenConstructorCensus`, `TestLeaseTokenCensusPlants` (5\n113|  shapes), `TestLeaseTokenUnforgeableOutsidePackage` all green in my run.\n114|- Own probe M4: build-tagged (`//go:build linux`) alias-backdoor plant —\n115|  census REJECTS it (KILLED, log `own/M4.log`). No build-tag hole in\n116|  `invcore.MustScanProduction`.\n117|\n118|## 5. Mutation — producer battery sampled, own plants added\n119|\n120|Producer `mutants.json` (in evidence tarball): 31 KILLED (30 N + 1 T),\n121|1 SURVIVED harmless control, NOT_APPLIED/COMPILE controls separate.\n122|Reviewer reran in isolated copies (logs attached):\n123|\n124|- `epoch` filter: N-presented-epoch, N-epoch-gte, N-epoch-lte — KILLED.\n125|- `census` filter: T-census-alias — KILLED with 264 `=== RUN` lines\n126|  (full behavioral suite executed alongside the census failure).\n127|- Own narrowings: M2 holder-malformed winner KILLED; M3 terminate live-owner\n128|  epoch-2 KILLED; B/C taxonomy KILLED (above); M4 census KILLED (above);\n129|  C2 harmless-comment SURVIVED control (applied).\n130|- M1/M1f SURVIVED with root-cause analysis (not a gate hole): admitting\n131|  epoch-0 for lease `zzz` is masked by the later lease-grammar arm (same\n132|  `invalid_arguments` class — defense in depth, log `own/M1.log`); admitting\n133|  epoch-0 for a valid but undriven lease (`leaseC`) survives only because no\n134|  test names the `{epoch 0, valid third lease}` vector. The epoch arm itself\n135|  is narrowed-and-killed by N-presented-epoch. Filed as P3 below.\n136|\n137|## 6. Agreement — 144 pairs, divergences killed both sides\n138|\n139|`TestLeaseTupleOrderAgreesWithSessstateCompare` enumerates\n140|3×2×2 per side = 144 pairs (lease IDs {x,y}, holders {a,b}, epochs\n141|{1,2,3}; holder/record/predecessor/checkpoint/reason varied to prove they\n142|never affect order). Both comparators read use only (epoch, lease_id);\n143|`created_at` is diagnostic-only per §5.3 and a member of neither comparator\n144|— the test comment discloses this substitution for the brief's\n145|created_at-ordering ask. Reviewer flipped the lease tie-break on each side\n146|in isolated copies: D1 (sessrepo) KILLED, D2 (sessstate) KILLED\n147|(logs `diverge/logs/D1*`, `D2*`).\n148|\n149|## 7. Traceability and docs — recomputed, not read\n150|\n151|- `go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck` rerun by reviewer: exit 0,\n152|  `acceptance_cases=110 bindings=57 clauses_discharged=28/485` — exactly the\n153|  claimed figures. The `reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256` re-pin matches\n154|  (tracecheck verifies the pin; green = match).\n155|- All 28 clause line references resolve into `SPEC.v0.6.0.md`; sampled\n156|  excerpts (5.3#1@1927, 5.3#2@1957, 2.2#1@408, 2.2#2@410, …) match the\n157|  pinned text verbatim.\n158|- 9 acceptance cases bind existing declarations (`Authorize`,\n159|  `AuthorizeActivation`, `AuthorizeTerminateStale`, `Bind`,\n160|  `CompareAndSwapLease`, `winningLeaseFor`, `AppendEvent`, `Reduce`,\n161|  `VerifyFencingToken`) to tests that drive them — no self-minted claim.\n162|- 5.3 at 7/8 partial (only caller-side union-maximum 5.3#5 open, disclosed);\n163|  2.2 at 4/22 sliver (replication/secret/store families disclosed as gaps).\n164|- README fencing section + figures (110/57/28/485) match my reproduced\n165|  tracecheck output; test/mutant commands verified runnable; no CLI,\n166|  doctor, or capability claim. LOGBOOK entry truthful.\n167|- Residual `section:17.2` gap prose predates this story and is unchanged —\n168|  correctly out of scope.\n169|\n170|## 8. Hygiene and gates — all rerun by reviewer\n171|\n172|- Changed paths = exactly the 22 CR paths (7 tracked modifications +\n173|  `internal/fencing/` untracked); no `__pycache__`/`.pyc`; no\n174|  `task-board.config.json`; no stray plants (worktree contains only the\n175|  candidate; my harnesses live in `/tmp`).\n176|- `go test ./internal/fencing/ -count=1`: ok, 40/40 PASS, 0 FAIL.\n177|- `go test ./internal/sessrepo/ ./internal/sessquery/ ./internal/sessstate/\n178|  -count=1`: all ok (sessquery 223s, sessstate 98s).\n179|- `go test ./internal/traceability/... -count=1`: ok.\n180|- `-race` all green, rerun by reviewer: fencing (5s), sessrepo (29s),\n181|  sessstate (90s), traceability/... (49s + 268s), sessquery (485s).\n182|- `go vet` (touched trees), `gofmt -l internal` (empty), `cataloggen\n183|  -check` (exit 0), `tracecheck` (exit 0), `git diff --check` (exit 0),\n184|  `go build ./...` (exit 0), `GOOS=windows go build` + `go vet` on\n185|  fencing/sessrepo/sessquery/sessstate (exit 0): all clean.\n186|- `TestGatesPerformNoDurableWrites` (byte-identical tree + identical\n187|  verdicts across two runs): green — purity bound holds, no crash seam.\n188|\n189|## Findings (advisory, non-blocking)\n190|\n191|- P3: add one vector to `TestAuthorizeRefusesMalformedPresented` —\n192|  `{session A, epoch 0, valid third lease}` expecting `invalid_arguments`\n193|  — so the M1f narrowing shape is pinned alongside N-presented-epoch.\n194|  Fits a sibling leaf or follow-up; not worth a respawn cycle alone.\n195|- P3: the `section:17.2` gap rationale (\"no ownership implementation\n196|  exists\") is now stale prose beside the new ownership code; consider\n197|  rewording to its narrower reader-enum meaning when that section is next\n198|  touched.\n199|\n200|## What was rerun vs accepted\n201|\n202|Reran myself: fencing/sessrepo/sessquery/sessstate/traceability suites\n203|(normal and -race, sessquery race 485s exit 0), tracecheck, cataloggen\n204|-check, vet, gofmt, `go build ./...`, GOOS=windows build/vet, `git\n205|diff --check`, forge/use builds, epoch + census mutant subsets, all own\n206|attacks (M1/M1f/M2/M3/A/B/C/C2/M4/D1/D2) with raw logs.\n207|Accepted from attached evidence: full 31/31 producer battery per-plant\n208|logs (sampled 4/31 by rerun) and the full `go test ./...` 27-package\n209|sweep from the CR validation log (touched-package equivalents rerun\n210|here).\n211|\n212|No product edits were made. Candidate left UNCOMMITTED as required.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
