{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cb79","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae9c-cde9-7503-b771-d867bf2eff64"},"sequence":1047,"recorded_at":1780531400002089,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"c50b0c1e-3e8f-47ac-b724-ccf66299a997","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"c50b0c1e-3e8f-47ac-b724-ccf66299a997","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"c50b0c1e-3e8f-47ac-b724-ccf66299a997"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0aea0-0123-7b43-8149-7bbfa0563db8"},"task_id":"01a0aea0-0123-7b43-8149-7bbfa0563db8","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0aea0-0123-7b43-8149-7bbfa0563db8","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-1oqfec/worktree/internal/sessrepo/lease_store.go`.\n(404 line(s) above)\n405|func (repository *Repository) WinningLease(sessionID string) (LeaseSummary, error) {\n406|\trepository.mutex.Lock()\n407|\tdefer repository.mutex.Unlock()\n408|\tview, err := repository.loadSessionLocked(sessionID)\n409|\tif err != nil {\n410|\t\treturn LeaseSummary{}, err\n411|\t}\n412|\tstored, err := repository.loadLeasesLocked(view.directory, view.record.sessionID)\n413|\tif err != nil {\n414|\t\treturn LeaseSummary{}, err\n415|\t}\n416|\tif len(stored) == 0 {\n417|\t\treturn LeaseSummary{}, refuse(ErrUnknownLease, \"no winning lease is established for session %s\", sessionID)\n418|\t}\n419|\treturn stored[len(stored)-1], nil\n420|}\n421|\n422|// VerifyFencingToken revalidates a presented fencing token against the\n423|// current head: the renewal step an owner repeats before accepting input,\n424|// starting a provider turn, publishing a checkpoint, pushing records, and\n425|// resuming after an interruption past the refresh interval (Section 5.3).\n426|// A token below the winning epoch is stale, one beyond it names no known\n427|// lease, a same-epoch token under another fencing ID loses the tie, and a\n428|// token from another holder is not the owner. A nil error renews the\n429|// authorization the token carries; it mints no new lease and mutates no\n430|// durable state.\n431|func (repository *Repository) VerifyFencingToken(sessionID string, token FencingToken) error {\n432|\tif token.Epoch == 0 {\n433|\t\treturn refuse(ErrInvalidLease, \"fencing token carries epoch 0, want an epoch at or above 1\")\n434|\t}\n435|\tif _, err := scalar.ParseUUIDv4(token.LeaseID); err != nil {\n436|\t\treturn refuse(ErrInvalidLease, \"fencing token lease %q is not a UUIDv4: %v\", token.LeaseID, err)\n437|\t}\n438|\tif _, err := scalar.ParseUUIDv7(token.HolderHostID); err != nil {\n439|\t\treturn refuse(ErrInvalidLease, \"fencing token holder %q is not a UUIDv7: %v\", token.HolderHostID, err)\n440|\t}\n441|\trepository.mutex.Lock()\n442|\tdefer repository.mutex.Unlock()\n443|\tview, err := repository.loadSessionLocked(sessionID)\n444|\tif err != nil {\n445|\t\treturn err\n446|\t}\n447|\tstored, err := repository.loadLeasesLocked(view.directory, view.record.sessionID)\n448|\tif err != nil {\n449|\t\treturn err\n450|\t}\n451|\twinner := LeaseSummary{}\n452|\tif len(stored) > 0 {\n453|\t\twinner = stored[len(stored)-1]\n454|\t}\n455|\tif token.Epoch < winner.Epoch {\n456|\t\treturn refuse(ErrStaleLeaseEpoch, \"fencing token epoch %d precedes winning epoch %d for session %s\", token.Epoch, winner.Epoch, sessionID)\n457|\t}\n458|\tif token.Epoch > winner.Epoch {\n459|\t\treturn refuse(ErrUnknownLease, \"fencing token epoch %d names no known lease for session %s\", token.Epoch, sessionID)\n460|\t}\n461|\tif token.LeaseID != winner.LeaseID {\n462|\t\treturn refuse(ErrLeaseConflict, \"fencing token lease %s loses to winning lease %s at epoch %d\", token.LeaseID, winner.LeaseID, winner.Epoch)\n463|\t}\n464|\tif token.HolderHostID != winner.HolderHostID {\n465|\t\treturn refuse(ErrLeaseHolderMismatch, \"fencing token holder %s is not winning holder %s for session %s\", token.HolderHostID, winner.HolderHostID, sessionID)\n466|\t}\n467|\treturn nil\n468|}\n469|\n470|// CheckFencingExpiry enforces the operational grant-expiry policy: a grant\n471|// older than the refresh interval lapses and its holder must revalidate\n472|// through VerifyFencingToken. The lease named by a lapsed grant stays\n473|// authoritative — expiry retires the cached authorization, never the\n474|// ownership — and a grant validated exactly at the interval boundary is\n475|// still current. A non-positive interval is not a policy: it refuses.\n476|func CheckFencingExpiry(grant FencingGrant, policy FencingPolicy, now time.Time) error {\n477|\tif policy.RefreshInterval <= 0 {\n478|\t\treturn refuse(ErrInvalidLease, \"fencing policy refresh interval must be positive\")\n479|\t}\n480|\tif now.Sub(grant.ValidatedAt) > policy.RefreshInterval {\n481|\t\treturn refuse(ErrFencingExpired, \"fencing grant for session %s lapsed; revalidate the fencing token\", grant.SessionID)\n482|\t}\n483|\treturn nil\n484|}\n485|\n486|// loadLeasesLocked reads every stored lease for one session directory in\n487|// tuple order. The blobs are truth: there is no lease index to skew, so a\n488|// crash can only leave a blob stored or not. Staged temps are ignored; any\n489|// other entry that fails to read, decode, attest, bind to the session, or\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
